comments.body:
There's very little usage of `hilite_operator`. E.g. there's one use of `hilite_operator` to hilite the string `" = "`, but there are also 9 occurences of `" = "` in Parser/* that go without hiliting.

Using hilite https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/blob/master/src/Parsers/ASTAssignment.h#L36

Not using hilite e.g. https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/blob/master/src/Parsers/Access/ASTSettingsProfileElement.cpp#L40

Just want to confirm that none of those are operators and it's not a mistake?

```
$ grep -rn "\" = \"" Parsers/*
Parsers/Access/ASTCreateQuotaQuery.cpp:63:        settings.ostr << " " << type_info.name << " = " << type_info.valueToString(max_value);
Parsers/Access/ASTSettingsProfileElement.cpp:40:        settings.ostr << " = " << applyVisitor(FieldVisitorToString{}, value);
Parsers/ASTAlterNamedCollectionQuery.cpp:33:                settings.ostr << " = " << applyVisitor(FieldVisitorToString(), change.value);
Parsers/ASTAssignment.h:33:        settings.writeOperator(" = ");
Parsers/ASTCreateNamedCollectionQuery.cpp:37:            settings.ostr << " = " << applyVisitor(FieldVisitorToString(), change.value);
Parsers/ASTCreateQuery.cpp:42:        s.ostr << (s.hilite ? hilite_keyword : "") << s.nl_or_ws << "ENGINE" << (s.hilite ? hilite_none : "") << " = ";
Parsers/ASTDictionary.cpp:121:        settings.ostr << it->name << " = " << applyVisitor(FieldVisitorToString(), it->value);
Parsers/ASTFunction.cpp:673:                "equals",          " = ",
Parsers/ASTSetQuery.cpp:37:        format.ostr << " = " << applyVisitor(FieldVisitorToString(), change.value);
Parsers/ASTSetQuery.cpp:59:        format.ostr << " = " << value;

```
